spu_lifter: publish a call bracket's return pc for the whole call.

The interpreter stops at ctx->drain_ret_pc when a callee's return lands mid-function, so the caller's host frame takes
the continuation back. Only the spu_drain_call loop set that value, so while a brsl/bisl callee ran from the call
itself it held the enclosing bracket's pc (or 0). Resistance 3's igjob_00DC0200 calls an unlifted handler through
`bisl`; the interpreter ran on through the caller's loop into the same call, each iteration nested another host frame,
and the depth guard halted the SPU at 2000. Its policy module then restarted on a job-overwritten local store: two
buckets waited for a bucket signal that never comes, one took a garbage doorbell, and level start hung.

Each bracket now saves the outer value, sets its own before the call and restores it after the drain. The handoff
fixture gains the direct-call case (it covered only the queued one), and a lifter self-check pins the emitted form.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

